<title>ITALY: Italy's SanPaolo plans share buyback.</title>
<headline>Italy's SanPaolo plans share buyback.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The board of Italian banking group San Paolo said it intended to ask shareholders for authorisation to buy and allocate its own shares and to create a reserve of 200 billion lire for the proposed share buyback.</p>
<p>A San Paolo statement said the shares from the proposed buyback would serve two purposes, firstly for stock market operations within the framework of its privatisation.</p>
<p>Secondly the buyback would allow the creation of a pool of shares to be used as a form of incentive in the eventual allocation of stock to employees of the bank.</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
</text>
